The rain stops.
I step out of the house.
I walk slowly and reach a market.
This is the Sunday market.
There is a lot of crowd here.
I came here five months ago.
Then this market used to feel very strange to me.
But now I like it.
I stop at a fruit stall.
There are small mangoes in front in the shop.
"Brother, how much for these mangoes?" I ask.
The shopkeeper says, "Madam, these mangoes are one hundred rupees a kilo."
There are some big mangoes at the back of the shop.
I ask, "And those big mangoes?"
The shopkeeper replies, "Those mangoes are from Ratnagiri."
"They are very expensive, they are two hundred rupees a kilo."
"Are these small mangoes sweet?" I ask.
"Yes Madam, these are very sweet," he says.
"Okay, please give me one kilo of these mangoes," I say.
I give him one hundred rupees and move ahead.
